  "description": "Maximize the value of an array by reversing exactly one subarray [i, j]. The value is defined as the sum of |nums[i] - nums[i+1]| for all valid i.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. total = sum(|nums[i] - nums[i+1]|)\n2. max_gain = 0\n3. For i in 0..n-2:\n4.   For j in i+1..n-1:\n5.     gain = |nums[i]-nums[j+1]| + |nums[i-1]-nums[j]| - |nums[i-1]-nums[i]| - |nums[j]-nums[j+1]|\n6.     max_gain = max(max_gain, gain)\n7. Return total + max_gain",
